    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nSome modules report a lot of information, which may be irrelevant to what the user is looking for.\n\nFor example, healthcheck for lsp reports the health for all enabled language servers. \n\n### Expected behavior\n\nSome mechanism to support narrowing down the scope of a plugins healthcheck. I'm not sure what a good syntax would be. For the sake of an example, using a forward slash which I dont think would introduce any breaking changes. \n\nIf the lsp healthcheck were to support this, a specific language server could be checked with\n`checkhealth vim.lsp/gopls`",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I think this is covered by:\n\n- https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/32162\n- https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/22796\n\nWe had implemented folding for healthchecks, but it was reverted https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/28232 . The door is still open for that, just need someone to think about how to do it given what we discovered in that discussion.\n\nI don't think \"parameters\" is the right approach, that's just like when an app introduces more \"options\" because the app developers can't figure out how to make things _good by default_: it puts the onus on the user to workaround the junk UX.",
